--- Verdict ---
NO RESPONSE — no 0x3016 bit made GPIO8_IO27 track 0x3019 on either sensor
Combined with iter2 (nothing drives the net), the reasonable reading
is that GPIO8_IO27 is NOT routed to the OV5640 pads: the name is
inherited from upstream coralmicro and means nothing on this board.
Coverage note: 0x3016 implements only bits 0x03, so the sweep did
exercise every pad-enable bit that physically exists — the masked
bits are not untested, they are absent.
Still not a mathematical proof: a FREX INPUT on the sensor never
drives anything, so it stays invisible to a test that listens.

